# Extra sections for batch 1 (inserted before each post's closing section)
EXTRA.update({
 'web-design-packages-sri-lanka': [
   ('questions', 'Questions to Ask Before You Pay', P(
     'A short conversation before you pay a deposit can prevent most problems. Use these questions with any web design company, including us, and ask for the answers in writing.') + ol([
     '<strong>How many pages are included,</strong> and what counts as a page? Does a blog post or product count?',
     '<strong>How many rounds of changes</strong> are included in the design and after the first draft?',
     '<strong>Who writes the content?</strong> If you supply it, when is it needed, and what happens if it is late?',
     '<strong>Which platform will be used,</strong> and will you be able to update the website yourself?',
     '<strong>What happens after launch?</strong> How long is support included, and what does it cover?',
     '<strong>What are the yearly costs</strong> from the second year, for the domain, hosting and maintenance?',
     '<strong>Who owns the website</strong> and the domain once the project is paid for?']) + P(
     'If a company cannot answer these clearly, that tells you something about how the project will go. Clear answers mean clear expectations, which is the best start for any website.')),
   ('roi', 'Think About Return, Not Just Cost', P(
     'It helps to think of a website as an investment rather than an expense. If your average customer is worth LKR 15,000 to your business, a website that brings in just two extra customers pays back a starter package within weeks. A business website that ranks on Google for your main services can bring enquiries every month for years.',
     'That is why the cheapest option is rarely the best value. A slow site with no SEO, no clear calls to action and no way to measure results might cost less upfront, but it brings fewer customers. Choose the package that gives your website the best chance of earning its cost back, and grow from there.',
     'Once your website is live, track the enquiries it brings using Google Analytics, Search Console and a simple note of how each new customer found you. After a few months you will know exactly what the website is worth to your business, and whether it is time to upgrade.')),
 ],
 'website-maintenance-sri-lanka': [
   ('backup', 'Backups: Your Safety Net', P(
     'Backups are the single most important part of maintenance. If your website is hacked, an update breaks something, or a server fails, a recent backup lets you restore everything quickly. Without one, you may have to rebuild the website from scratch.',
     'A good backup routine follows three rules. First, backups run automatically on a schedule, not only when someone remembers. Second, they include both the website files and the database, which holds your pages, products and orders. Third, at least one copy is stored somewhere other than the website’s own server, so a server problem cannot destroy the backups too.',
     'Finally, backups must be tested. A backup that has never been restored is only a hope. Ask your provider when they last tested a restore, and how long a full restore would take.')),
   ('hacked', 'What to Do if Your Website Is Hacked', ol([
     '<strong>Do not panic and do not delete everything.</strong> Evidence helps find how the attacker got in.',
     '<strong>Change all passwords</strong> for hosting, the admin panel, the database and email.',
     '<strong>Restore a clean backup</strong> from before the problem started, if one exists.',
     '<strong>Update all software</strong> and remove unused plugins or old files.',
     '<strong>Scan the website</strong> to make sure no malicious code remains.',
     '<strong>Check Google Search Console</strong> for security warnings and request a review once the site is clean.']) + P(
     'Recovering from a hack takes time and money, and it can damage your reputation with customers and Google. Regular maintenance makes it far less likely to happen in the first place, which is why it is worth the small monthly cost.')),
   ('budget', 'How Much to Budget for Maintenance', P(
     'Maintenance costs depend on the size and type of website, how often it changes and how quickly problems need to be fixed. A small brochure website needs much less work than an online store that takes payments every day.',
     'When planning your yearly website budget, include three items: domain renewal, hosting renewal and maintenance. Together they keep your website online, secure and current. Read our guide on <a href="domain-and-hosting-sri-lanka.html">domain and web hosting in Sri Lanka</a> to understand the first two.')),
 ],
 'domain-and-hosting-sri-lanka': [
   ('email', 'Professional Email on Your Domain', P(
     'One of the best benefits of owning a domain is professional email. An address such as <em>sales@yourbusiness.lk</em> looks far more trustworthy than a free webmail address, and customers are more likely to reply to quotes and invoices sent from it.',
     'Business email can be provided by your hosting company or by a dedicated email service. Hosting email is affordable and fine for small teams. Dedicated services cost more per user but offer larger mailboxes, better spam filtering and reliable delivery. Either way, set up the email records correctly so your messages do not land in spam folders.')),
   ('renew', 'Renewals: Do Not Lose Your Domain', P(
     'Domain expiry is one of the most avoidable problems for a business. When a domain expires, the website and email stop working, and after a grace period the name can be released for anyone to register. Some businesses have lost names they used for years this way.',
     'Protect yourself by turning on automatic renewal where possible, keeping the registrar contact email up to date, and registering for several years if your budget allows. Put the renewal date in your calendar with a reminder a month before.')),
   ('speed', 'How Hosting Affects Speed and SEO', P(
     'Hosting quality has a direct effect on how fast your pages load. Slow servers delay the first byte of every page, and no amount of design work can fully hide that. Google measures real loading speed through Core Web Vitals, and slow websites tend to lose both rankings and visitors.',
     'Choose hosting with modern hardware, caching and a content delivery network for images when your audience is spread across countries. Our upcoming guide to website speed explains the other factors, such as image sizes and code, that you can improve on top of good hosting.')),
 ],
 'payment-gateway-sri-lanka': [
   ('fees', 'Understanding Fees and Pricing', P(
     'Gateway fees are usually a percentage of each successful payment, sometimes with a small fixed amount per transaction. Some providers also charge setup fees, annual fees or extra charges for foreign cards. When you compare providers, calculate the real cost using your expected monthly sales, not only the headline rate.',
     'Remember to include fees in your pricing. Many stores build them into product prices or delivery charges rather than adding a separate card fee, which can put customers off at checkout. Whatever you decide, keep pricing clear and consistent so customers are never surprised.')),
   ('steps', 'Step-by-Step: Adding Payments to Your Website', ol([
     '<strong>Choose your methods:</strong> card payments, cash on delivery, bank transfer and instalments.',
     '<strong>Prepare your website:</strong> products, prices, delivery information and all required policies.',
     '<strong>Apply to the gateway</strong> with your business documents and bank details.',
     '<strong>Integrate the gateway</strong> into your checkout using a plugin or the provider’s API.',
     '<strong>Test in sandbox mode</strong> with test cards, including failed and cancelled payments.',
     '<strong>Go live</strong> and place a small real order to confirm everything works end to end.',
     '<strong>Monitor payouts</strong> and reconcile orders with settlements every week.'])),
   ('abandon', 'Reduce Abandoned Carts', P(
     'Many customers add items to the cart and never pay. Some were only browsing, but many leave because of friction: a surprise delivery fee, a payment that failed, or a checkout that was hard to use on a small screen.',
     'Watch where people drop off, keep the number of steps low, show trust signals such as the padlock and payment logos, and follow up abandoned carts by email where customers have agreed to it. Small improvements to the checkout often bring more extra sales than a large advertising budget.')),
 ],
 'google-business-profile-sri-lanka': [
   ('photos', 'Photos That Win Customers', P(
     'Profiles with real, recent photos tend to get more clicks and calls. Customers want to see what they will get: your shop front so they can find you, the inside of your premises, your team, and examples of your work or products.',
     'Use bright, sharp photos taken on a good phone. Add new ones every month, especially after you finish a project worth showing. Avoid stock images, which look generic and can be removed by Google. For service businesses, before-and-after photos and short videos of completed jobs work particularly well.')),
   ('posts', 'Use Posts to Stay Active', P(
     'Google Business Profile lets you publish short updates with a photo and a button, such as “Call now” or “Learn more”. Use them to announce offers, seasonal services, new products, events and recent projects. Posts show customers that the business is active and give them a reason to contact you today.',
     'A simple rhythm is one post a week. Link each post to the most relevant page on your website, such as the service page or a new blog article, so interested customers can read more and make an enquiry.')),
   ('multi', 'Businesses With More Than One Location', P(
     'If you have several branches, each real location that serves customers can have its own profile with its own address, phone number and opening hours. Link each profile to a page on your website for that branch, with its address, map, photos and local information.',
     'Do not create profiles for places where you do not have staff or premises. Google treats this as spam, and it can lead to suspension of all your listings.')),
 ],
})
